WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:16.235
Buffalo Academy, dedicated to the memory of Elizabeth March, opened its doors three months later.

2
00:00:16.236 --> 00:00:23.593
People came from town and from neighboring cities near and far to satisfy their curiosity about the new establishment.

3
00:00:23.594 --> 00:00:33.221
"It's a nice turnout, isn't it?" Mr. Laurence said proudly as he waved at a few familiar faces and warmly greeted those he didn't know as well.

4
00:00:33.222 --> 00:00:40.414
Mother kept wiping tears from her eyes as she said over and over again, "Beth would be so happy."

5
00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:49.313
Jo, along with Amy and Laurie, happily served drinks and snacks to the visitors and directed all those who had questions to Professor Bauer.

6
00:00:49.314 --> 00:00:56.540
Meg gave tours of the place while John minded the children and made sure they didn't eat more cookies than they should.

7
00:00:56.541 --> 00:01:04.493
"I desperately need a cold drink," the Professor gasped as he politely detached himself from a group of mothers

8
00:01:04.494 --> 00:01:08.553
who had gathered to pepper him with questions about the school curriculum.

9
00:01:08.554 --> 00:01:14.575
Handing him a tall glass of lemonade, Jo asked, "Do you think it's going to be a success?"

10
00:01:14.576 --> 00:01:20.238
Looking at her tenderly, the Professor remarked, "Jo, whatever you do will succeed.

11
00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:26.953
Do you know why?" Without waiting for an answer, he replied, "Because you put your whole soul into it."

12
00:01:26.954 --> 00:01:33.788
Laurie and Amy exchanged knowing glances as they predicted another wedding in the March family soon.

13
00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:39.550
At present, however, the Professor's very words, like a prophecy, were about to come true.

14
00:01:39.551 --> 00:01:45.376
A young delivery boy ran up to the refreshment table asking for Josephine March.

15
00:01:45.377 --> 00:01:47.703
"That's me," she replied.

16
00:01:47.704 --> 00:01:52.079
"Package for you, ma'am," the boy said, handing her a thick envelope.

17
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.506
"What is it, Jo?" Amy asked curiously.

18
00:01:55.507 --> 00:01:59.850
"I don't know," Jo said as she ripped the envelope open.

19
00:01:59.851 --> 00:02:09.363
Inside was a bound book, and when Jo saw the title and author's name, she let out a cry, "It's my novel!"

20
00:02:09.364 --> 00:02:14.993
The Professor caught her arm to steady her while Amy took the book from Jo's hands.

21
00:02:14.994 --> 00:02:20.856
"The Little Women: A Story About Life, by Jo March," she read.

22
00:02:20.857 --> 00:02:25.635
"Jo! This is your book! Your book's been published!"

23
00:02:25.636 --> 00:02:32.211
Hearing Amy's excited voice and Laurie's cheers, Meg came running, followed by their parents.

24
00:02:32.212 --> 00:02:37.883
When Laurie held up the book, everyone clapped and shouted their congratulations loudly.

25
00:02:37.884 --> 00:02:41.995
"See, Jo, another success," whispered the Professor.

26
00:02:41.996 --> 00:02:46.526
"Your soul is in that book, just as it is in this school."

27
00:02:46.527 --> 00:02:52.540
Jo took his hand without saying a word, because he already knew what she wanted to say.

28
00:02:52.541 --> 00:02:58.249
The grand opening of Buffalo Academy brought greater results than anyone had thought.

29
00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:04.846
It was obvious that the upcoming days would be busy with accepting applications and planning lessons.

30
00:03:04.847 --> 00:03:09.339
John quit his job and took on a position as an English teacher.

31
00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:15.774
Amy volunteered to work part-time as the art instructor, and Meg said she would teach a sewing class.

32
00:03:15.775 --> 00:03:24.473
Aside from the other teachers who were hired, Buffalo Academy was the joint effort of the March, Laurence, and Brooks families uniting as one.

33
00:03:24.474 --> 00:03:30.844
As she pondered that, Jo decided it would be a good chance for her to spend some private time with her sisters.

34
00:03:30.845 --> 00:03:35.515
They agreed to take a walk together, just the three of them, down to the pond.

35
00:03:35.516 --> 00:03:42.324
"This has really been an eventful day," Meg said when they reached the pond and sat on a fallen log.

36
00:03:42.325 --> 00:03:46.690
"My legs are killing me," said Amy, rubbing her sore feet.

37
00:03:46.691 --> 00:03:51.588
"But I'd gladly stand for weeks if it means making this school a success."

38
00:03:51.589 --> 00:03:58.001
The girls sat together watching a few ducks swim around the pond as the sun was sinking in the sky.

39
00:03:58.002 --> 00:04:04.488
"We used to come out here a lot when we were younger, but I haven't been for so long," said Meg.

40
00:04:04.489 --> 00:04:11.447
"Remember how we used to swim in the water, and Jo would grab our legs and try to pull us under?" giggled Amy.

41
00:04:11.448 --> 00:04:17.288
"Then you'd run home and tell Mother or Father what I did and get me in trouble," Jo pointed out.

42
00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:22.625
"We were so young and carefree," Amy said with a smile on her face.

43
00:04:22.626 --> 00:04:29.262
"That's why we did so many foolish things," Meg said, blushing at the memory of some of her embarrassing moments.

44
00:04:29.263 --> 00:04:34.566
"But look at us now, girls," said Jo. "Meg is a mother with two children.

45
00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:38.677
Amy is married to Laurie and may soon start a family of her own."

46
00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:45.978
"And Jo is an accomplished writer and headmistress of the most prestigious school in America," Amy added with pride.

47
00:04:45.979 --> 00:04:50.618
"By the way, you never told us what your book is about, Jo," said Meg.

48
00:04:50.619 --> 00:04:55.574
Looking out at the pond, Jo took a moment to gather her thoughts before answering,

49
00:04:55.575 --> 00:05:01.930
"It's about dreams and failures, growing up and growing pains, love and heartache,

50
00:05:01.931 --> 00:05:08.851
opportunities and memories, regrets and hope, birth and death . . . It's about life."

51
00:05:08.852 --> 00:05:14.614
The sisters grew silent as they watched the sun slowly disappear below the horizon.

52
00:05:14.615 --> 00:05:20.712
"I miss her so much," Amy said, choking up as her mind filled with memories of Beth.

53
00:05:20.713 --> 00:05:27.264
As they used to do when they were younger, the girls wrapped their arms around each other and cried.

54
00:05:27.265 --> 00:05:31.797
"Beth wouldn't want us to cry every time we think of her," sniffed Amy.

55
00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:34.767
"You're right," Meg said, wiping her eyes.

56
00:05:34.768 --> 00:05:40.075
"Beth was always a positive, happy girl, and that's how I want to remember her."

57
00:05:40.076 --> 00:05:47.006
"Remember how she used to always get excited whenever we started a new chapter in a book?" asked Jo.

58
00:05:47.007 --> 00:05:54.927
Giggling at the memory, Amy said, "She said new chapters are the best because there is so much to look forward to."

59
00:05:54.928 --> 00:05:59.933
Jo dried her eyes and looked at her sisters. "What do you say, girls?

60
00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:05.852
Let's tell each other about the new chapters in our lives that are about to begin," she suggested.

61
00:06:05.853 --> 00:06:12.556
Meg started first. "My new chapter begins with Daisy and Demi starting school at Buffalo Academy.

62
00:06:12.557 --> 00:06:20.572
While they learn how to become good citizens, I will learn how to be a better mother, wife, daughter, and sister."

63
00:06:20.573 --> 00:06:27.794
"My new chapter begins with finding a house for me and Laurie to live in," said Amy, and laughed along with her sisters.

64
00:06:27.795 --> 00:06:33.468
"Then each day I want to do something that will touch the life of another person in some way,

65
00:06:33.469 --> 00:06:39.923
whether through my words, actions, instructions as a teacher, or even through my paintings."

66
00:06:39.924 --> 00:06:49.769
Finally it was Jo's turn. "My new chapter begins with the start of a new outlook on life, on relationships, on goals, and on myself.

67
00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:56.877
I hope to treasure each moment as it deserves to be valued and love each person as they deserve to be loved."

68
00:06:56.878 --> 00:07:05.669
Hugging each other tightly, the March sisters were grateful for each other and for the chance to bond even more closely as they grew older together.

69
00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:12.497
"Well, girls, it looks as if this day is almost over," said Amy, looking up at the darkening sky.

70
00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:17.357
"A new day waits for us tomorrow," said Meg, standing up to leave.

71
00:07:17.358 --> 00:07:25.772
As Jo followed her sisters back to the house, she added, "and a new chapter in this story called life."

72
00:07:25.773 --> 00:07:54.614
[caption_out@
